{"key": "averitec/dev/21", "dataset": "averitec", "split": "dev", "original_index": 21, "claim": "Taylor Zundel claimed on Instagram that she and other early voters in Utah, were unable to cast ballots in the 2020 presidential elections, as they were told they had already voted.", "claim_date": "27-10-2020", "gold_label": "Refuted", "results": {"hero2": {"status": "ok", "predicted_label": "Not Enough Evidence", "label_correct": false, "qa_pairs": [{"question": "Does the evidence provided contain any information regarding Taylor Zundel's Instagram claims about voting in Utah?", "answer": "No, the provided evidence does not contain any information regarding Taylor Zundel's Instagram claims about voting in Utah. The evidence focuses on Senator Christian Kitchell's background and her run for ASCSN Student Body President.", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/ASCSNStudentGovernment/posts/hey-coyotes-meet-senator-christian-kitchell-kitchell-is-running-for-ascsn-studen/2920227871353855/", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Question: Did Taylor Zundel claim on Instagram that early voters in Utah were prevented from voting in the 2020 presidential election?", "answer": "Based on the evidence provided, it is impossible to determine whether Taylor Zundel made that claim. The provided text discusses President Trump's response to a moderator's question regarding the QAnon movement and does not contain any information regarding Taylor Zundel, Instagram, or voting issues in Utah during the 2020 presidential election.", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/CBS2Boise/posts/on-thursday-night-the-moderator-asked-president-trump-if-he-would-disavow-qanon-/3782996491712029/", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Does the evidence provide any information regarding Taylor Zundel's claim that early voters in Utah were unable to cast ballots in the 2020 presidential election?", "answer": "No, the provided evidence does not contain any information regarding Taylor Zundel's claim or any reports of early voters in Utah being unable to cast ballots in the 2020 presidential election. The evidence focuses exclusively on social media reactions to Joe Biden's announcement as a presidential candidate.", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/ksltv/posts/its-official-ex-vp-joe-biden-is-running-for-president-which-democratic-candidate/10157699536088676/", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Does the evidence provided support or relate to Taylor Zundel's claim regarding voter suppression in Utah?", "answer": "No, the evidence provided does not support or relate to Taylor Zundel's claim. The evidence consists of a Facebook post from 2017 regarding LGBTQ inclusion in the United Methodist Church, which is entirely unrelated to the 2020 presidential elections or voter suppression in Utah.", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/groups/progressivemethodists/posts/946969988739807/", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Did Taylor Zundel's Instagram claim regarding early voters in Utah being unable to cast ballots in the 2020 presidential election appear in the provided collection of articles and commentary?", "answer": "No, Taylor Zundel's Instagram claim regarding early voters in Utah being unable to cast ballots in the 2020 presidential election does not appear in the provided evidence. The provided text is a description of a collection of articles and commentary focused on themes such as global instability, government surveillance, geopolitical tensions, and various fringe theories, but it does not contain any mention of Taylor Zundel or voting issues in Utah.", "url": "https://realtruthblog.com/current-quicklinx-2", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Does the evidence provided relate to Taylor Zundel's claim regarding voter eligibility in Utah during the 2020 presidential elections?", "answer": "No, the provided evidence does not relate to Taylor Zundel's claim. The evidence discusses the release of a trailer for a new Amazon Prime Video series titled *World's Toughest Race: Eco-Challenge Fiji* hosted by Bear Grylls.", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/FijiEmbassyJakarta/posts/amazon-just-released-a-new-trailer-for-the-worlds-toughest-race-eco-challenge-fi/592133581499996/", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "What is the connection between Taylor Zundel's Instagram claim regarding Utah voters and the commentary on the United Methodist Church?", "answer": "Based on the provided evidence, there is no connection between Taylor Zundel's Instagram claim regarding Utah voters and the commentary on the United Methodist Church. The evidence provided only discusses Pastor Kevin Miller's comparison regarding the rift within the United Methodist Church and the subsequent social media commentary.", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/nwitimes/posts/first-united-methodist-church-of-valparaiso-pastor-kevin-miller-likened-the-curr/10157969101479413/", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Question: Did Taylor Zundel claim on Instagram that she and other early voters in Utah were unable to cast ballots in the 2020 presidential elections because they were told they had already voted?", "answer": "Based on the provided evidence, there is no information to confirm or deny whether Taylor Zundel made such a claim on Instagram. The evidence provided pertains exclusively to a public letter shared by Matthew Gong regarding his personal journey as a queer individual.", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/clpauthor/posts/birthday-letter-from-the-queer-son-of-an-lds-apostle-this-public-letter-posted-y/2499493093498591/", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Does the evidence provided relate to Taylor Zundel's claim regarding voting in Utah?", "answer": "No, the provided evidence does not relate to Taylor Zundel's claim. The evidence pertains to a Facebook post from MRC Middle School Naxxar regarding School Council Elections in 2019, whereas the claim concerns Taylor Zundel's Instagram post regarding the 2020 presidential elections in Utah.", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/MRCMiddleSchoolNaxxar/posts/check-your-emails-for-further-information-related-to-the-upcoming-school-council/2098569420224602/", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "What is the relationship between Taylor Zundel's claim regarding voting in Utah and the involvement of religious and corporate organizations in refugee resettlement?", "answer": "Based on the provided evidence, there is no relationship between Taylor Zundel's claim regarding voting in Utah and the involvement of religious and corporate organizations in refugee resettlement. The evidence focuses exclusively on the various entities involved in refugee resettlement and does not contain any information regarding Taylor Zundel or voting claims in Utah.", "url": "https://patriotmongoose.wordpress.com/2016/10/page/3/", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}], "justification": "**Step-by-step justification:**\n\n1.  **Analyze the Claim:** The claim asserts that a specific individual, Taylor Zundel, made a specific statement on Instagram regarding voter suppression (being told they had already voted) in Utah during the 2020 presidential election.\n2.  **Evaluate the Evidence:** I have reviewed all ten provided question-answer pairs (Q1 through Q10).\n3.  **Check for Relevance:** \n    *   Q1 states the evidence discusses Senator Christian Kitchell.\n    *   Q2 states the evidence discusses President Trump and the QAnon movement.\n    *   Q3 states the evidence discusses social media reactions to Joe Biden's candidacy.\n    *   Q4 states the evidence discusses LGBTQ inclusion in the United Methodist Church.\n    *   Q5 states the evidence discusses global instability and geopolitical tensions.\n    *   Q6 states the evidence discusses an Amazon Prime Video series.\n    *   Q7 states the evidence discusses the United Methodist Church.\n    *   Q8 states the evidence discusses a public letter by Matthew Gong.\n    *   Q9 states the evidence discusses School Council Elections in 2019.\n    *   Q10 states the evidence discusses refugee resettlement.\n4.  **Determine the Verdict:** Across all provided evidence, there is zero mention of Taylor Zundel, her Instagram account, or any voting issues in Utah related to the 2020 election. Because the evidence does not contain any information that could either prove or disprove the claim, it is impossible to reach a conclusion.\n\n**Label:** Not Enough Evidence", "admitted_sources": [{"url": "https://www.facebook.com/ksltv/posts/its-official-ex-vp-joe-biden-is-running-for-president-which-democratic-candidate/10157699536088676/", "date": "2016-02-01", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.facebook.com/FijiEmbassyJakarta/posts/amazon-just-released-a-new-trailer-for-the-worlds-toughest-race-eco-challenge-fi/592133581499996/", "date": "2000-01-01", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.facebook.com/ASCSNStudentGovernment/posts/hey-coyotes-meet-senator-christian-kitchell-kitchell-is-running-for-ascsn-studen/2920227871353855/", "date": "2000-01-01", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.facebook.com/groups/progressivemethodists/posts/946969988739807/", "date": "2000-01-01", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.facebook.com/nwitimes/posts/first-united-methodist-church-of-valparaiso-pastor-kevin-miller-likened-the-curr/10157969101479413/", "date": "2000-01-01", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://realtruthblog.com/current-quicklinx-2", "date": "2018-10-09", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.facebook.com/MRCMiddleSchoolNaxxar/posts/check-your-emails-for-further-information-related-to-the-upcoming-school-council/2098569420224602/", "date": "2000-01-01", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://patriotmongoose.wordpress.com/2016/10/page/3/", "date": "2016-10-07", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.facebook.com/CBS2Boise/posts/on-thursday-night-the-moderator-asked-president-trump-if-he-would-disavow-qanon-/3782996491712029/", "date": "2000-01-01", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.facebook.com/groups/41742591337/posts/10157167989186338/", "date": "1999-01-01", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.facebook.com/clpauthor/posts/birthday-letter-from-the-queer-son-of-an-lds-apostle-this-public-letter-posted-y/2499493093498591/", "date": "2000-01-01", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}], "legacy_scores": {"question_hu_meteor": 0.7016690973910225, "qa_hu_meteor": 0.3921775526713799}, "error_category": null, "source_output_sha256": "543cf392cfcf3e9c13e6c80dc2f531dcff15e17c774aaa469d1ce852b8921b0c", "qa_source_note": null}, "sanctuary": {"status": "ok", "predicted_label": "Not Enough Evidence", "label_correct": false, "qa_pairs": [{"question": "What was the specific allegation made by Taylor Zundel on Instagram regarding the 2020 presidential election in Utah?", "answer": "No Evidence.", "url": null, "source_status": "no_source_link", "placeholder": true}, {"question": "How did Utah election officials respond to the claims of voters being told they had already voted?", "answer": "SALT LAKE CITY — With Election Day less than two weeks away, thousands of Utah registered voters have already begun casting their ballots. With so many high-profile offices at stake, elevated voter turnout is expected, so state elections officials are making a concerted effort to safeguard the integrity of the process. “Of registered voters, we received about 15.5% at this point — which is just under 260,000 voters,” said Utah Elections Director Justin Lee. They also corrupt the essence of our representative form of government,” Huber said. “Whether a Utah voter is mailing in a ballot or voting in person, anyone who has specific information about election fraud or discrimination should pass that information on to my office or to the FBI.” Lee said, thus far, there have been no major problems in Utah regarding voting irregularities, but the state is cooperating to certify all properly cast ballots. “Before big federal elections, the Justice Department is always on alert and ready in case there are any issues,” he said.", "url": "https://www.deseret.com/utah/2020/10/21/21525969/utah-early-voting-open-vote-in-person-election-2020/", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "Was there any documented evidence of widespread voter disenfranchisement in Utah during the 2020 early voting period?", "answer": "\"In 2018 we only had two small counties that were not vote by mail, and those two counties came on board for the Super Tuesday Presidential Primary in March. We have not had to do any significant expansion of vote by mail in 2020. We have not experienced any issue with widespread voter fraud in Utah. In Utah’s most populous county, voter turnout is already at a robust level, with about 16% of ballots already cast, said Lannie Chapman, Salt Lake County chief deputy clerk. “People are really (submitting) their ballots and dropping them in drop boxes,” she said. “(On Oct. 20), we started early voting and the amount of people that have come and participated in the early voting — we haven’t seen numbers like this in a very long time, since before vote by mail was the primary way that we held elections (in 2014). SALT LAKE CITY — With Election Day less than two weeks away, thousands of Utah registered voters have already begun casting their ballots. With so many high-profile offices at stake, elevated voter turnout is expected, so state elections officials are making a concerted effort to safeguard the integrity of the process. “Of registered voters, we received about 15.5% at this point — which is just under 260,000 voters,” said Utah Elections Director Justin Lee.", "url": "https://abcnews.com/Politics/election-officials-dozens-states-dispute-president-trumps-claim/story?id=71833120", "source_status": "linked_not_entailment_verified", "placeholder": false}, {"question": "What was the context of the claim made by Taylor Zundel on October 27, 2020?", "answer": "No Evidence.", "url": null, "source_status": "no_source_link", "placeholder": true}, {"question": "Did the Utah Secretary of State confirm the claims made by Zundel regarding early voters?", "answer": "No Evidence.", "url": null, "source_status": "no_source_link", "placeholder": true}], "justification": "Reasoning:\n1. The claim asserts that on October 27, 2020, Taylor Zundel posted on Instagram claiming that she and other early voters in Utah were prevented from voting in the 2020 presidential election because they were incorrectly told they had already cast their ballots.\n2. Regarding the specific allegation (Q1), there is no evidence found to confirm the existence of the Instagram post or the specific wording used by Zundel. Regarding the context (Q4) and the response from the Utah Secretary of State (Q5), no evidence was found to support or confirm these specific claims.\n3. While the evidence provided (Q2, Q3) discusses the general state of Utah's election integrity—noting that Utah Elections Director Justin Lee stated there were \"no major problems in Utah regarding voting irregularities\" and that officials were working to safeguard the process—this information is general and does not directly address or debunk the specific individual claim made by Taylor Zundel. There is a gap between the general reports of election stability and the specific existence/content of the social media claim.\n4. Because there is no evidence provided to confirm that the Instagram post actually occurred (Q1, Q4) and no evidence to confirm the specific details of the claim, it is impossible to verify if the event described in the claim took place. The evidence provided discusses the broader election environment but fails to address the specific subject of the claim.\n\nLabel: Not Enough Evidence", "admitted_sources": [{"url": "https://www.facebook.com/ksltv/posts/its-official-ex-vp-joe-biden-is-running-for-president-which-democratic-candidate/10157699536088676/", "date": "2016-02-01", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.facebook.com/ASCSNStudentGovernment/posts/hey-coyotes-meet-senator-christian-kitchell-kitchell-is-running-for-ascsn-studen/2920227871353855/", "date": "2000-01-01", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.facebook.com/groups/progressivemethodists/posts/946969988739807/", "date": "2000-01-01", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://www.facebook.com/nwitimes/posts/first-united-methodist-church-of-valparaiso-pastor-kevin-miller-likened-the-curr/10157969101479413/", "date": "2000-01-01", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://realtruthblog.com/current-quicklinx-2", "date": "2018-10-09", "date_class": "strict_ok", "date_policy": "v2-revision-exclusion-20260916"}, {"url": "https://patriotmongoo